Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.47,0:00:09.30,Default,,0,0,0,,YAMU!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.38,0:00:11.76,Default,,0,0,0,,YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.85,0:00:12.75,Default,,0,0,0,,YAMU!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.39,0:00:31.43,Default,,0,0,0,,You're on a move!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.65,0:01:06.67,Default,,0,0,0,,If you honestly believe you can win, then\Nstop talking about it and do it already.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.07,0:01:09.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you really think\Nwhat Yugi said is true?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.73,0:01:14.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Does he have some sort of card combination\Nthat can destroy the three Egyptian gods?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.15,0:01:18.31,Default,,0,0,0,,It's your move.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.75,0:01:21.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's see this plan of\Nyours. With pleasure.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.37,0:01:25.61,Default,,0,0,0,,First, I'll play my\NMagnet Reverse Magic card.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.69,0:01:28.95,Default,,0,0,0,,This allows me to choose any\Nrock or machine monster that was
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.03,0:01:32.97,Default,,0,0,0,,destroyed this turn and bring it\Nback to the field in defense mode!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.19,0:01:36.51,Default,,0,0,0,,So I've chosen my Valkyra!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.81,0:01:40.87,Default,,0,0,0,,And since I've summoned a monster,\NSlifer's special effect activates!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.01,0:01:42.73,Default,,0,0,0,,So give me your best shot!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.11,0:01:50.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Unfortunately for you,\Nthanks to my trap card,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.45,0:01:53.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Slifer's blast is\Nredirected to your obelisk!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.95,0:02:01.25,Default,,0,0,0,,He's gone. One down,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.53,0:02:03.91,Default,,0,0,0,,two more to go Now Valkyra,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.11,0:02:09.77,Default,,0,0,0,,separate But why would he do that?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.13,0:02:12.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Because every time Yugi gets a new monster
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.39,0:02:15.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Slifer the Sky Dragon\Nis forced to strike it
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.97,0:02:26.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Too bad But once again,\Nmy trap card kicks in!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.81,0:02:29.11,Default,,0,0,0,,So now Slifer's blast backfires!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.33,0:02:42.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.24,0:02:43.07,Default,,0,0,0,,No way!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.15,0:02:45.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess Yugi really did\Nhave a plan after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.21,0:02:47.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you see that?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.63,0:02:51.09,Default,,0,0,0,,He beat the Egyptian gods in one move?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.23,0:02:53.89,Default,,0,0,0,,And I never expected\Nany less from you, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.07,0:02:59.71,Default,,0,0,0,,He did it, he did it, he's better\Nthan the Pharaoh. No offense,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.89,0:03:03.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course. The funny thing\Nabout it is, there's no way I
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.41,0:03:05.91,Default,,0,0,0,,could have destroyed those\Nmonsters without your help,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.99,0:03:07.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Pharaoh You see,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.31,0:03:11.19,Default,,0,0,0,,all the battles we've been through together\Ntaught me something Defeating someone
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.27,0:03:16.15,Default,,0,0,0,,who wields a strong force Often means\Nusing that very force against them So
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.23,0:03:20.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I knew the only way I could take down\Nyour three Egyptian gods Was to figure
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.71,0:03:25.42,Default,,0,0,0,,out a way to attack them with their own\Npower So that's exactly what I just did.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.65,0:03:27.35,Default,,0,0,0,,And the rest is history.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.29,0:03:29.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Excellent work, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.71,0:03:34.39,Default,,0,0,0,,By trusting your instincts, you were able\Nto accomplish the seemingly impossible.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.47,0:03:37.94,Default,,0,0,0,,You destroyed the most powerful\Ncreatures in Duel Monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.71,0:03:42.89,Default,,0,0,0,,But remember, that doesn't mean\Nthat you've won the game. True.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.25,0:03:44.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Not yet, anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.77,0:03:47.31,Default,,0,0,0,,So in the meantime, let's\Nsee what you've got.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.39,0:03:48.35,Default,,0,0,0,,All right,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.71,0:03:53.71,Default,,0,0,0,,but I should warn you, I have plenty of\Ntricks left, and I'll start with this,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.97,0:03:56.51,Default,,0,0,0,,my Polymerization Magic Card.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.31,0:04:03.77,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'll use it to merge my Gazelle and\Nmy Berfomet together to form Chimera.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.01,0:04:06.03,Default,,0,0,0,,the Flying Mythical Beast!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.95,0:04:09.93,Default,,0,0,0,,No way!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.25,0:04:11.19,Default,,0,0,0,,What a comeback!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.47,0:04:13.94,Default,,0,0,0,,That's the strongest monster on the field!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.39,0:04:15.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Chimera!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.17,0:04:18.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Attack Alpha the Magnate Warrior!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.43,0:04:19.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Pulverizing Pouch!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.45,0:04:30.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like you're down\Nto two monsters now.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.93,0:04:31.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Impressive!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.01,0:04:35.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Even though he lost his three best\Ncards, the Pharaoh bounced right back!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.83,0:04:37.59,Default,,0,0,0,,And now he's got the upper hand again!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.67,0:04:39.15,Default,,0,0,0,,No, not quite.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.51,0:04:40.34,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.42,0:04:42.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi may have fewer life points,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.79,0:04:45.01,Default,,0,0,0,,but he managed to come\Nup with an unprecedented
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.09,0:04:47.75,Default,,0,0,0,,strategy to defeat the Egyptian god cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.99,0:04:50.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I've never seen anything like that before.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.41,0:04:52.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I can see now that I was wrong, Mukuba.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.29,0:04:55.59,Default,,0,0,0,,He is the king of games. Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.01,0:04:56.97,Default,,0,0,0,,You mean that?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.25,0:04:58.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Say, what?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.37,0:05:01.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Am I going nuts or did Kaiba\Njust admit that he was wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.95,0:05:04.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Where was I? Oh, yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.33,0:05:11.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I was about to sacrifice my Beta and\NGamma warriors in order to bring out this!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.39,0:05:12.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Buster Blader!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.41,0:05:19.63,Default,,0,0,0,,This duel is quite a close race.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.05,0:05:24.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Just when I think the Pharaoh is back\Nin the lead again, Yugi speeds ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.21,0:05:25.77,Default,,0,0,0,,But only one thing counts.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.19,0:05:29.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Crossing the finish line\Nfirst, and my money's on Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.45,0:05:32.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, it's go time!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.09,0:05:34.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Buster Blader, attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.25,0:05:36.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Destroy his Chimera!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.33,0:05:51.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Well done, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.77,0:05:54.73,Default,,0,0,0,,But unfortunately for\Nyou, not well enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.53,0:05:58.61,Default,,0,0,0,,You just triggered\NChimera's special effect, so
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.69,0:06:01.15,Default,,0,0,0,,now i can bring back one\Nof the two monsters i
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.23,0:06:04.53,Default,,0,0,0,,merged together to form\Nchimera and i choose this
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.61,0:06:09.27,Default,,0,0,0,,one the mighty burplement\Nshow yourself my beast
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.41,0:06:13.69,Default,,0,0,0,,and i'm afraid there's plenty\Nmore where that came from
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.25,0:06:20.73,Default,,0,0,0,,so let's see what else you've\Ngot pharaoh very well your
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.81,0:06:24.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Buster Blader may be powerful,\Nbut it's not indestructible.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.57,0:06:27.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, say hello to my new friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.95,0:06:31.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I sacrifice Burkomet to summon...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.61,0:06:33.67,Default,,0,0,0,,...Beast of Guilford!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.79,0:06:39.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I shall place one card\Nface down and end my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.31,0:06:41.93,Default,,0,0,0,,The Pharaoh's lost it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.07,0:06:46.73,Default,,0,0,0,,He just summoned a monster to the field\Nthat's weaker than Yugi's. Unless...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.81,0:06:49.75,Default,,0,0,0,,he wants Yugi to destroy\Nhis monster so the Pharaoh
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.83,0:06:52.71,Default,,0,0,0,,can turn around and activate\Nits special ability.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.71,0:06:57.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey's got a point there, but that's\Na risk I'm gonna have to take.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.79,0:06:59.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Because it could be even more dangerous to
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.07,0:07:02.78,Default,,0,0,0,,let the Barrow keep that\Nmonster on the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.83,0:07:05.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Alright, my move.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.73,0:07:08.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll place this face\Ndown and then I'll send
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.19,0:07:11.01,Default,,0,0,0,,your Guilfer on a one-way\Ntrip to the graveyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.01,0:07:16.31,Default,,0,0,0,,So here goes, Buster Blader,\NDragon Sword, attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.33,0:07:26.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid you've just activated my\NBeast of Guilford special effects.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.17,0:07:28.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Whenever it's sent to the graveyard,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.93,0:07:33.65,Default,,0,0,0,,it decreases the attack strength of\None of your monsters by 500 points.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.23,0:07:41.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess I'll end my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.65,0:07:43.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought you might say that.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.31,0:07:45.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I place one card face down,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.99,0:07:49.93,Default,,0,0,0,,and then I'll activate a magic card\Nknown as Awakening from Beyond.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.19,0:07:51.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Here's how it works.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.53,0:07:55.24,Default,,0,0,0,,My opponent earns the right to\Ndraw two cards, and in exchange,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.35,0:07:59.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I earn the right to transfer one\Nmonster from my graveyard to my hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.07,0:08:02.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Now go ahead and draw your cards, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.17,0:08:06.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Now it's my turn!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.85,0:08:09.77,Default,,0,0,0,,So one of my monsters returns to the game.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.49,0:08:11.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, but which one?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.97,0:08:16.77,Default,,0,0,0,,But besides the Egyptian gods, what's the\Nmost powerful monster in his graveyard?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.75,0:08:18.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Best of luck, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.01,0:08:21.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Now,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.92,0:08:24.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll start by discarding\None card from my hand
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.41,0:08:27.33,Default,,0,0,0,,in order to summon a\Nmonster known as the Tricky.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.67,0:08:31.55,Default,,0,0,0,,But bringing back the\NTricky would be pointless.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.07,0:08:32.95,Default,,0,0,0,,First of all,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.27,0:08:36.59,Default,,0,0,0,,the Pharaoh would have to remove a card\Nfrom his hand in order to summon it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.67,0:08:38.67,Default,,0,0,0,,And even if he did,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.95,0:08:43.65,Default,,0,0,0,,It still wouldn't be strong enough to\Ndefeat my Buster Blader. What's wrong,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.87,0:08:46.47,Default,,0,0,0,,trying to guess what\Nmonster I brought back?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.63,0:08:51.91,Default,,0,0,0,,You won't You see, Yugi, it's a\Nmonster you didn't even know I had
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.81,0:08:56.85,Default,,0,0,0,,And now I shall summon this\Ncreature to the field in attack mode
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.59,0:09:02.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Swift Gaia the First Light, come forth\NHow did Dad get in his graveyard?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.05,0:09:10.39,Default,,0,0,0,,And although it's a level 7 monster,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.73,0:09:15.55,Default,,0,0,0,,it can be summoned without a sacrifice\Nbecause it's the only card left in my hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.83,0:09:16.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.83,0:09:19.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I never sent that card to the graveyard!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.37,0:09:20.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, that's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.81,0:09:21.75,Default,,0,0,0,,But I did.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.91,0:09:23.99,Default,,0,0,0,,At the very start of our duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.83,0:09:29.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Before I summoned my first monster,\NI got rid of a card in my hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.51,0:09:33.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait a sec!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.73,0:09:38.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you telling me you sent Gaia to\Nthe graveyard all the way back then?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.45,0:09:42.73,Default,,0,0,0,,But why would you throw away such a\Npowerful card so early in the duel?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.43,0:09:45.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I was preparing for this.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.57,0:09:49.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I have known from the very beginning\Nthat we would get to this point.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.67,0:09:50.50,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.58,0:09:52.58,Default,,0,0,0,,But how could you have predicted that?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.83,0:09:54.05,Default,,0,0,0,,It was simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.37,0:09:57.02,Default,,0,0,0,,From the moment I chose\Nthe cards in my deck,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.11,0:09:59.70,Default,,0,0,0,,I knew the course that\Nthis duel would take.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.95,0:10:04.31,Default,,0,0,0,,For although I held the three most\Npowerful monsters in existence,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.75,0:10:06.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I knew that I needed more.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.87,0:10:14.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi, what I'm saying is, I knew\Nyou would defeat the Egyptian gods!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.25,0:10:17.47,Default,,0,0,0,,That's impossible!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.89,0:10:21.54,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no way he could have\Nknown how all this would go down!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.13,0:10:27.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi, destroying the three Egyptian gods\Nwas merely the first step of this ritual.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.59,0:10:29.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Now that they're gone,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.37,0:10:33.49,Default,,0,0,0,,the true test of our readiness to\Nseparate from one another can begin.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.99,0:10:38.76,Default,,0,0,0,,So if you're ready to live on your own,\Nthen prove it to me by winning this duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.79,0:10:44.43,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, Gaia, annihilate his Buster\NGlader with Spiral Let's Thrust Attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.25,0:10:53.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi, there is only one soul with the\Npower to save the Pharaoh, and that is you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.63,0:10:58.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Only by defeating him can you release\Nhis spirit to its final resting place.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.83,0:11:01.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, be strong.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.49,0:11:17.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you alright?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.09,0:11:19.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's hope so.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.27,0:11:21.79,Default,,0,0,0,,You just activated my face down card!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.87,0:11:23.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Soul Rope!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.39,0:11:27.73,Default,,0,0,0,,It lets me summon a monster from my\Ndeck to replace the one I just lost!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.93,0:11:30.11,Default,,0,0,0,,As long as I give up 1,000 points!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.39,0:11:33.47,Default,,0,0,0,,So now, let's see which\Ncard I should choose!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.01,0:11:34.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Aha!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.07,0:11:36.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I play this!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.77,0:11:38.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Witch of the Black Forest!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.77,0:11:40.89,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'm putting her in defense mode!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.01,0:11:45.73,Default,,0,0,0,,But Yugi, that's hardly\Nenough to protect you!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.57,0:11:49.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Why would he give up 1,000\Npoints just to play that?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.87,0:11:50.77,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.85,0:11:54.61,Default,,0,0,0,,It seems like he might be getting\Ndesperate out there, no joke.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.85,0:11:59.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess Yugi just realized there's\Nno way he can win. Not a chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.25,0:12:03.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sure this is all\Npart of Yugi's strategy.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.43,0:12:08.03,Default,,0,0,0,,He summoned that witch for a\Nreason I know to sacrifice it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.17,0:12:10.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course to play something stronger
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.69,0:12:15.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll take it from here. Watch this.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.09,0:12:17.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm trading my witch for my summon skull
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.95,0:12:22.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on out, old pal!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.33,0:12:28.99,Default,,0,0,0,,And whenever my Witch of the Black\NForest goes to the graveyard,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.07,0:12:32.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I can transfer a monster\Nfrom my deck to my hand!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.31,0:12:34.71,Default,,0,0,0,,And I choose my old pal, Marshmallow!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.99,0:12:35.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Well done.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.29,0:12:38.11,Default,,0,0,0,,There's a move I didn't expect.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.57,0:12:40.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.53,0:12:43.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Two of Yugi's strongest\Nmonsters face-to-face in battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.69,0:12:46.22,Default,,0,0,0,,The whole thing's pretty\Nbizarre, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.31,0:12:47.91,Default,,0,0,0,,You think it's weird for us?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.99,0:12:51.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Just think about how the\NPharaoh and Yugi must feel.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.75,0:12:54.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Here we go, Summon Skull!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.17,0:12:57.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Attack his fierce knight now!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.55,0:12:58.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Lightning strike!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.51,0:13:16.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like your life points are wide open.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.17,0:13:18.85,Default,,0,0,0,,But luckily for you, my move's over.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.13,0:13:23.87,Default,,0,0,0,,This duel could be the most\Ndifficult challenge I've ever faced.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.95,0:13:26.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Ever since I was reborn into this world,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.67,0:13:30.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi has been behind me,\Nsupporting me, giving me strength.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.99,0:13:34.69,Default,,0,0,0,,But now, for the first time,\Nhe's facing me as an opponent.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.11,0:13:38.43,Default,,0,0,0,,And I have to believe that\NYugi feels the same way I do,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.93,0:13:43.23,Default,,0,0,0,,staring into the face of his\Nclosest friend and greatest rival.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.95,0:13:47.57,Default,,0,0,0,,But like Yugi, I need to fight\Nharder than I've ever fought before.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.65,0:13:50.53,Default,,0,0,0,,and do everything in my\Npower to win this battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.37,0:13:56.41,Default,,0,0,0,,It's my move, and the card that I'm about\Nto draw is the exact one that I need.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.79,0:14:00.95,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, Almighty Big\NShield Gardener, come back!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.77,0:14:04.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's see if I was correct!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.07,0:14:10.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Alright, now I've seen it all.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.05,0:14:12.27,Default,,0,0,0,,That's nuts.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.61,0:14:15.11,Default,,0,0,0,,How could he have known what\Ncard he was going to draw?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.19,0:14:18.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I suppose that's what they\Nmean by luck of the draw.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.17,0:14:19.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Not quite.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.11,0:14:21.35,Default,,0,0,0,,That move had nothing to do with luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.71,0:14:26.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Truth is, he knew exactly what\Ncard he was about to draw. What?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.27,0:14:28.09,Default,,0,0,0,,But their decks were shuffled, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.17,0:14:29.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Can he see the future?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.93,0:14:34.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Because if he can, I'd say that qualifies\Nas an unfair advantage. You're wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.01,0:14:38.85,Default,,0,0,0,,You see, the Pharaoh didn't predict\Nwhat his next card would be.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.97,0:14:40.49,Default,,0,0,0,,His willpower made it so.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.05,0:14:43.85,Default,,0,0,0,,It appears the Pharaoh's\Ndetermination was so strong.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.93,0:14:46.73,Default,,0,0,0,,he actually influenced\Nfate with his own will.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.67,0:14:49.73,Default,,0,0,0,,That's insane!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.05,0:14:52.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Since when can fate be controlled?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.41,0:14:55.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, Pea, if I've learned anything\Nfrom hanging out with Yugi,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.89,0:14:57.71,Default,,0,0,0,,it's that nothing's impossible.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.31,0:15:00.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I believe it's your move.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.97,0:15:02.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Sounds good to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.93,0:15:05.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll start by activating Pot of Greed!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.91,0:15:07.43,Default,,0,0,0,,And you know what that means!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.51,0:15:09.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I get to draw two new cards!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.27,0:15:12.93,Default,,0,0,0,,And then, I summon my waterbond!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.29,0:15:15.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't blink, you just might miss him!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.83,0:15:18.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Because I've sacrificed him to play this!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.05,0:15:22.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Curse of Dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.23,0:15:25.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi's moving up in the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.23,0:15:27.29,Default,,0,0,0,,He's got two powerhouses now.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.71,0:15:29.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Now summon skull, attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.53,0:15:34.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi's monster's too weak,\Nso why would he attack?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.79,0:15:40.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Trust me, he knows what he's doing
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.87,0:15:42.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's hope so.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.21,0:15:49.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Say what?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.45,0:15:51.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Told you it was all good You see,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.43,0:15:55.79,Default,,0,0,0,,By attacking Big Shield Gardener,\NYuki switched it into attack mode.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.77,0:16:01.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Now it's my dragon's turn.\NAttack his Big Shield Gardener.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.35,0:16:11.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Now your last line of defense is gone
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.11,0:16:19.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi's having the time of his life up\Nthere And who could blame him If he wins,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.89,0:16:22.83,Default,,0,0,0,,that means he's ready to\Nface the world on his own
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.25,0:16:25.61,Default,,0,0,0,,And the Pharaoh will finally be free
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.27,0:16:31.25,Default,,0,0,0,,What's up, Taya?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.69,0:16:32.93,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't watch anymore
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.91,0:16:35.29,Default,,0,0,0,,If the Pharaoh loses,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.63,0:16:39.35,Default,,0,0,0,,this is the last time we'll ever\Nsee him I don't know about you guys,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.43,0:16:41.55,Default,,0,0,0,,but I'm not ready to say goodbye yet
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.19,0:16:44.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Please make them stop, Taya.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.75,0:16:49.03,Default,,0,0,0,,this isn't easy for any of us,\Nbut that duel has to go on Plus,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.13,0:16:53.66,Default,,0,0,0,,you know as well as I do, we couldn't\Nstop this thing if we tried I guess so,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.77,0:16:55.99,Default,,0,0,0,,But remind me why. Here's the deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.29,0:17:00.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything that's happened since those\Ntwo met has been leading up to this.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.41,0:17:01.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Just think about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.83,0:17:04.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Every single duel that\NYugi and the Pharaoh ever
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.33,0:17:06.99,Default,,0,0,0,,faced together was\Npreparing them for this one.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.07,0:17:09.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Every enemy they ever stared down.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.31,0:17:11.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Every strategy they ever planned.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.27,0:17:14.79,Default,,0,0,0,,And every friend they ever saved\Nhelped shape who they are today.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.87,0:17:18.16,Default,,0,0,0,,And now they need this test\Nto see how far they've come.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.31,0:17:20.14,Default,,0,0,0,,But why?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.59,0:17:22.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Because when they first met,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.43,0:17:26.29,Default,,0,0,0,,these guys had a lot to learn, and\Nthey needed each other to get by.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.37,0:17:30.37,Default,,0,0,0,,But hopefully by now they're both\Nready to move on with their lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.45,0:17:33.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Trust me, Taya, this duel\Nis really all for the best.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.75,0:17:38.16,Default,,0,0,0,,And as tough as it may seem, we need\Nto support those two guys all the way.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.35,0:17:40.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.75,0:17:44.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I can sense the presence of\Nan old friend in my deck,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.17,0:17:47.19,Default,,0,0,0,,and it's time for us to reunite.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.59,0:17:49.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I may be defenseless now.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.05,0:17:51.87,Default,,0,0,0,,But that's all about to change.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.35,0:17:53.27,Default,,0,0,0,,My move!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.63,0:17:58.91,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, I activate a magic card\Nknown as Dark Magic Curtain!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.83,0:18:01.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Next,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.74,0:18:03.90,Default,,0,0,0,,I shall give up half my\Nlife points in order to
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.99,0:18:07.41,Default,,0,0,0,,summon my greatest creature\Nand most faithful servant!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.75,0:18:10.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Come forth, Dark Magician!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.05,0:18:24.43,Default,,0,0,0,,i was afraid he'd do that now yugi's\Nforced to fight against his favorite
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.51,0:18:30.77,Default,,0,0,0,,monster well i'm glad i stuck around i'm\Nnot done yet next i activate my face down
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.85,0:18:35.51,Default,,0,0,0,,card book of secret arts which raises\Nthe attack strength of my dark magician
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.59,0:18:41.59,Default,,0,0,0,,by 300 points now
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.67,0:18:43.51,Default,,0,0,0,,dark magician destroy
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.59,0:18:46.91,Default,,0,0,0,,his summon skull with dark magic attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.15,0:19:00.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Nice work.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.63,0:19:01.55,Default,,0,0,0,,My king,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.87,0:19:06.83,Default,,0,0,0,,I have journeyed 5,000 years across time\Nand space to serve you in this battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.09,0:19:10.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Is something wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.71,0:19:13.63,Default,,0,0,0,,No, just nerves, I guess.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.95,0:19:16.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Dark Magician,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.45,0:19:18.92,Default,,0,0,0,,your arrival has sparked a strange vision,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.11,0:19:22.23,Default,,0,0,0,,but what are these memories\Nof old that haunt me?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.75,0:19:29.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi, this is the strongest monster I\Nhave left, and you know him quite well.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.29,0:19:36.13,Default,,0,0,0,,So if you intend to defeat me today,\Nyou must first defeat my Dark Magician!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.97,0:19:41.53,Default,,0,0,0,,If I want to save my closest friend,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.81,0:19:44.93,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm going to have to destroy\Nmy most trusted monster!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.35,0:20:17.21,Default,,0,0,0,,YOLA! YOLA! YOLA!
